          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sslash G
            is a bit like the quotient set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/G
            (the set of
            = succeed "-orbits)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in the same
            = succeed "-orbit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+resolution"} resolution
            of the usual quotient. When the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            fails to be free, the action groupoid is generally better-behaved than the quotient set.
          %p
            The action groupoid also goes by other names, including ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+quotient"}> weak quotient
            ’. It is a special case of a ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo+colimit"}> pseudo colimit
            ’, as explained below. It is also called a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"}> semidirect product
            ” and then written
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \rtimes G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on a groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acts on a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            it also acts on the fundamental groupoid of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This notion generalises to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+actions"} monoid actions
            = succeed "." do
              %strong action category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_category_theory In category theory
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon S \times G \to S
            of a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on the set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %em action groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sslash G
            (or, more precisely,
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ⫽
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sslash_\rho G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            for which:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an object is an element of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                a morphism from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s' \in S
                is a group element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %mi s
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g s = s'
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi s
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,s) \colon s \to g s
            %li
              %p
                The composite of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi s
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,s) \colon s \to g s = s'
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi s
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mi s
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (g',s')\colon
                      s' \to g's'
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi s
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                        %mi g
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g' g, s) \colon s \to g' g s
          %p
            Equivalently, we may define the
            %em action groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sslash G
            to be the groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mo ×
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi s
                              %mo ≔
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mn 1
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mrow
                              %mi t
                              %mo =
                              %mi ρ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; S \times G
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{s \coloneqq p_1}\swarrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\searrow^{t = \rho}
                  \\\
                  S
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  S
                  }
          %p with composition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S \times G) \times_{t,s} (S \times G) \simeq S \times G \times G \to S \times G
          %p
            given by the product in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            We can denote the morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\sslash G
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi s
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\sslash G \coloneqq \{s\stackrel{g}{\to} \rho(s,g)  | s\in S, g\in G\}.
          %h3#in_1category_theory In (∞,1)-category theory
          #ActionInfinityGroupoid.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be an (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              ,1)-category, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\in Grpd(C)
              be a groupoid object in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
              be an object. Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mo →
                              %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi G
                                  %mn 0
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi p
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇉
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi G
                                  %mn 0
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\cdots
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset{\to}{\to}{\to}
                    \&amp;
                    X\times_{G_0}G\times_p G
                    \&amp;
                    \\rightrightarrows
                    \&amp;
                    X\times_{G_0}G
                    \&amp;
                    \\to
                    \&amp;
                    X
                    }
            %p such that the degree-wise projections give a simplicial map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mo →
                              %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi G
                                  %mn 0
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi p
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇉
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi G
                                  %mn 0
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mo →
                              %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi p
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇉
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\cdots
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset{\to}{\to}{\to}
                    \&amp;
                    X\times_{G_0}G\times_p G
                    \&amp;
                    \\rightrightarrows
                    \&amp;
                    X\times_{G_0}G
                    \&amp;
                    \\to
                    \&amp;
                    X
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^a
                    \\\
                    \\cdots
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset{\to}{\to}{\to}
                    \&amp;
                    G\times_p G
                    \&amp;
                    \\rightrightarrows
                    \&amp;
                    G
                    \&amp;
                    \\xrightarrow{p}
                    \&amp;
                    G_0
                    }
            %p
              is called an
              %em action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %em on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi colim
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim\; X\times_{G_0}^{\times_\bullet}
              is called
              %em
                action
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %em on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#interpretations Interpretations
          %p On top of the above explicit definitions, there are several useful ways to think of action groupoids.
          %p
            Recall that the action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is equivalently thought of as a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sets
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho \colon \mathbf{B}G \to Sets
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            regarded as a one-object groupoid, denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            This functor sends the single object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            to the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h3#as_a_pseudo_colimit As a pseudo colimit
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\sslash G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-colimit
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mi ρ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S\sslash G \simeq colim_{\mathbf{B}G} \rho
                  \\,.
          %p The universal cocone consists of cells of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi ρ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⇐
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⫽
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\rho(g)}{\to}&amp;&amp; S
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\Leftarrow}&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; S\sslash G
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the 2-morphism is uniquely specified and in components given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \mapsto (s \stackrel{g}{\to} \rho(s,g))
          %h3#as_associated_universal_bundle As associated universal bundle
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_*
            be the category of pointed sets and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sets
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sets
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sets_* \to Sets
            be the canonical forgetful functor. We can think of this as the “universal
            = succeed "-bundle\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\sslash G
            is the pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⫽
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Sets
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                          %mi Sets
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S\sslash G
                  \&amp;\to&amp;
                  Sets_*
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}G
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\rho}{\to}&amp;
                  Sets
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            One place where we discussed this is the comment
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2007/08/on_hess_and_lack_on_bundles_of_1.html#c019094"} It was David Roberts who apparently first noticed…
          %p
            Notice also that an action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            gives rise to a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋊
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon S \rtimes G \to G
            which has the property of unique path lifting, or in other words is a discrete opfibration. It is also called a covering morphism of groupoids, and models nicely covering maps of spaces.
          %p
            Higgins used this idea to lift presentations of a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to presentations of the covering morphism of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            derived from the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on cosets, and so to apply graph theory to obtain old and new subgroup theorems in group theory.
          %h3#as_a_stack As a stack
          %p
            In the case where the action is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to sets with structure, such as internal to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            one wants to realize the action groupoid as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
            which then usually goes by the same name
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\sslash G
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_representation_theory Relation to representation theory
          %p
            The action groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\sslash G
            of a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            come equipped with a canonical map to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G \simeq \ast \sslash G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} slice
            of groupoids over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            to the actions that they arise from.
          %p
            For more on this see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-action"} infinity-action
            and also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles"} geometry of physics – representations and associated bundles
          %h2#ActionooGrpd
            Action
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            All of this goes through almost verbatim for actions in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            in that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            with a single object. An action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho \colon \mathbf{B}G \to (\infty,1)Cat
          %p
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} (∞,1)Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            to some
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            Again we want to
            %strong define
            the
            %em action groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\sslash G
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} (∞,1)-categorical colimit
            over the action:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo →
                  %mi ρ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
